  <entry>
    <title>Fixing GitHub Access in China with Git Proxy Settings</title>
    <link href="/2025/08/31/weekend/"/>
    <url>/2025/08/31/weekend/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Developers in China often face connectivity issues when trying to access GitHub. Here’s a common error I encountered, even with my Clash proxy app running:</p><figure class="highlight vhdl"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs vhdl">fatal: unable <span class="hljs-keyword">to</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">access</span> <span class="hljs-symbol">&#x27;https</span>://github.com/SwallowGo/SwallowGo.github.io.git/&#x27;: Failed <span class="hljs-keyword">to</span> connect <span class="hljs-keyword">to</span> <span class="hljs-number">123.0</span>.<span class="hljs-number">0.1</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">port</span> <span class="hljs-number">7890</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">after</span> <span class="hljs-number">21069</span> ms: Couldn<span class="hljs-symbol">&#x27;t</span> connect <span class="hljs-keyword">to</span> server<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>The issue is that the <code>git</code> command-line tool often does not use the system’s proxy settings automatically. After some research, I found the solution is to configure Git’s proxy settings directly.</p><p>The essential commands to set a global proxy for Git are:</p><figure class="highlight stylus"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs stylus">git config <span class="hljs-attr">--global</span> http<span class="hljs-selector-class">.proxy</span> http:<span class="hljs-comment">//127.0.0.1:7890</span><br>git config <span class="hljs-attr">--global</span> https<span class="hljs-selector-class">.proxy</span> http:<span class="hljs-comment">//127.0.0.1:7890</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>This configuration works for all your workspaces because it’s set globally. This change is persistent and will not be reset by restarting your computer.</p><p>To cancel these proxy settings later, run the following commands:</p><figure class="highlight stylus"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs stylus">git config <span class="hljs-attr">--global</span> <span class="hljs-attr">--unset</span> http<span class="hljs-selector-class">.proxy</span><br>git config <span class="hljs-attr">--global</span> <span class="hljs-attr">--unset</span> https.proxy<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure>]]></content>
    
    
    <categories>
      
      <category>study</category>
      
    </categories>
    
    
  </entry>
  
  
  
